  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You were bred, raised, and <strong>commissioned</strong> inside a Spires patron-house as an Aesthetic-Class asset - displayed, never taught, groomed for a life of being looked at and listened to. You learned how the powerful talk to each other when they think no one is measuring them, how to open a locked door with nothing but bearing and a smile, and exactly how far charm carries before someone checks your paperwork.</p><p>Then your talent surfaced as a \"malfunction,\" and the house that made you started drafting the decommission order. You ran. You kept the old talk-your-way-in life - the poise, the contacts, the reflex of belonging - and now you rent it out from the Grid as a deniable contractor, paying cash to stay off Mama Cassavir's leash.</p>",
      "director": ""
    },
